.TH DHCPD 8 "October 2026" "go-dhcpd 1.8.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
dhcpd \- go-dhcpd DHCP and BootP server daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dhcpd
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-o | \-\-stdout ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dhcpd
is the go-dhcpd daemon, a DHCP and BootP server implementing RFC 2131,
RFC 2132, and related option-format RFCs. It allocates dynamic and static
IPv4 leases, tracks them in a local SQLite3 database, and exposes a REST
API for monitoring and administration.
.PP
The daemon binds a raw AF_PACKET socket to receive broadcast DHCP traffic
from clients that do not yet have an IP address (source 0.0.0.0), in
addition to a conventional UDP socket on port 67 for unicast and
relay-agent traffic. Because raw sockets and binding to port 67 both
require elevated privileges,
.B dhcpd
must be run as root, or with the
.B CAP_NET_RAW
and
.B CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE
capabilities.
.PP
Subnet and static-lease definitions are not read directly by the daemon.
Instead they are supplied by an external "config-provider" plugin,
configured via the
.B plugins.config_provider
section of the configuration file and invoked by the daemon as a
subprocess for each request (see
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5)
and the
.B PLUGINS
section below).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Path to the JSON5 configuration file to load. Defaults to
.IR /etc/go-dhcpd/config.json5 .
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-stdout
Write log output to standard output instead of syslog. Intended for
development and debugging; production deployments should rely on the
default syslog logging.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version, author, copyright, and license information, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary, then exit.
.SH PLUGINS
.B dhcpd
loads exactly one config-provider plugin at startup, named by
.BR plugins.config_provider.name " in the configuration file. Two plugins"
are bundled:
.TP
.B file-config
Reads the
.B subnets
and
.B static
arrays from the daemon's own configuration file (or another file named by
the plugin's
.B config_path
setting). This plugin is read-only: API requests that would modify
subnets or static hosts are rejected with
.B 403 Forbidden
while it is active. See
.BR go\-dhcpd\-file\-config (3)
for the plugin's full interface.
.TP
.B sqlite3-config
Stores subnets and static hosts in a SQLite3 database named by the
plugin's
.B db_path
setting, and supports full create/read/update/delete access through the
REST API. See
.BR go\-dhcpd\-sqlite3\-config (3)
for the plugin's full interface.
.PP
Existing
.B subnets
and
.B static
data can be moved from a configuration file into a
.B sqlite3-config
database with
.BR go\-dhcpd\-migration\-tool (8)
before switching
.B plugins.config_provider.name
from
.B file-config
to
.BR sqlite3-config .
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Initiate a graceful shutdown: the DHCP listeners are closed and the
process exits. The lease database is not altered on shutdown.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The daemon exited normally, either via
.B \-\-help
or
.BR \-\-version ,
or by receiving a shutdown signal after running successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Startup failed: the configuration could not be loaded, the lease database
could not be opened, the config-provider plugin could not be loaded, or
the DHCP server could not be created.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/go-dhcpd/config.json5
Default configuration file (see
.BR \-\-config ).
.TP
.I /etc/go-dhcpd/config.json5.example
Annotated example configuration, installed alongside the real
configuration file by
.BR "make install" .
.TP
.I /var/lib/go-dhcpd/dhcpd.db
Default lease-tracking SQLite3 database, named by
.B global.database_path
in the configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/go-dhcpd/plugins/
Default directory searched for config-provider plugin binaries when
.B plugins.config_provider.path
is not set in the configuration file. The actual prefix is whatever
.B INSTALL_PREFIX
was used at build/install time.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/go-dhcpd
PAM service used to authenticate HTTP Basic Auth credentials presented to
the REST API's authenticated endpoints.
.SH NETWORK API
The daemon exposes a REST API, by default on TCP port 18467 (see
.BR global.api_port ).
.BR /health ", " /version ", and " /metrics
are always unauthenticated; every other endpoint requires HTTP Basic Auth
verified against the host's local accounts via PAM, and can additionally
be served over TLS by setting
.B global.tls.enabled
in the configuration file. See
.I Docs/API.md
in the go-dhcpd source distribution for the full endpoint reference.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-migration\-tool (8),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-file\-config (3),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-sqlite3\-config (3)
